+---
+id: task-001-fix-sku-case-free-shipping-at-50.00-vat-rounding
+type: task
+title: "Fix SKU case, free shipping at 50.00, VAT rounding"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+Three reports on the order service:
+
+1. Lower-case SKU (`lb-220`) refused as unknown; SKUs are case-insensitive (README, Products).
+2. Goods of exactly €50.00 after discounts were charged shipping; README says free from €50.00.
+3. Line VAT one cent low (€1.99 at 22% gave €0.43, expected €0.44); README says round half up per line.
+
+## Done
+
+- `Catalog.find` now uses `canonicalSku` (src/catalog.ts).
+- `shippingCost` uses `>=` for the free-shipping threshold (src/shipping.ts).
+- `lineVat` uses `percentOf` (half up) instead of floor (src/tax.ts).
+- Tests added in test/orders.test.ts (lower-case SKU, 49.99 vs 50.00 boundary, 0.5-cent VAT rounding).
diff --git a/src/catalog.ts b/src/catalog.ts
